## Why This Is Asked
Tests ability to design multi-tenant inference with strict data residency, budgets, and auditable lineage in a real-world GCP setup.

## Key Concepts
- Tenant isolation in Vertex AI Endpoints and Feature Store namespaces
- Routing logic with per-tenant budget and latency SLAs
- Data Catalog metadata tagging for lineage and governance
- Drift detection and rollback triggers per tenant

## Code Example
```javascript
// Pseudo routing function
async function routeRequest(tenantId, req) {
  const budgetOk = checkBudget(tenantId);
  const latencyOk = checkLatency(tenantId);
  const endpoint = budgetOk && latencyOk ? getTenantEndpoint(tenantId) : getSharedEndpoint();
  return await predict(endpoint, req);
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you enforce per-tenant quotas in Feature Store and endpoints?
- How would you simulate rollback scenarios and validate audit trails?

## Why This Is Asked
Tests practical multi-plant deployment, data/model versioning, drift monitoring, canary strategy, and cost governance on GCP.

## Key Concepts
- Multi-tenant data architecture and versioning strategies
- Vertex AI custom training pipelines and endpoint management
- Pub/Sub, Dataflow, BigQuery integration patterns
- Drift detection algorithms and automated rollback mechanisms
- Per-tenant resource quotas and cost-aware autoscaling

## Code Example
```javascript
// Example: update endpoint traffic split for canary deployment
const aiplatform = require('@google-cloud/aiplatform');
const client = new aiplatform.v1.EndpointServiceClient();

async function updateTrafficSplit(endpointPath, newModelId, trafficPercentage) {
  const [endpoint] = await client.getEndpoint({ name: endpointPath });

  const deployedModels = endpoint.deployedModels.map(model => ({
    id: model.id,
    ...model
  }));

  const trafficSplit = {
    '0': (100 - trafficPercentage) / 100, // existing model
    '1': trafficPercentage / 100          // new canary model
  };

  await client.deployModel({
    endpoint: endpointPath,
    deployedModel: {
      model: `projects/${project}/locations/${location}/models/${newModelId}`,
      displayName: `plant-a-canary-${Date.now()}`,
      trafficSplit
    }
  });
}
```

## Implementation Considerations
- Data versioning: Implement BigQuery table partitioning and Dataflow snapshot windows
- Model registry: Use Vertex AI Model Registry with semantic versioning per plant
- Drift monitoring: Set up custom metrics and Cloud Monitoring alerts
- Rollback automation: Cloud Functions triggered by drift thresholds
- Cost controls: Per-project budgets and Vertex AI endpoint autoscaling policies
